<exercise>
    <introduction>
        <p>
        Sue keeps practicing basketball but never improves. The probability that
      Sue makes a basket is always 0.2. Let <m>X</m> be the number of shots it
      takes until Sue makes a basket.    
        </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="0.5in">
    <statement>
        <p>
            How is <m>X</m> distributed?
        </p>
    </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace=".5in">
    <statement>
        <p>
           What is the pmf of <m>X</m>?
        </p>
    </statement>
    </task>

     <task workspace=".5in">
    <statement>
        <p>
            How many shots do you expect Sue to take before she makes her first
            basket?
        </p>
    </statement>
    </task>
     <task workspace=".5in">
    <statement>
        <p>
            What is the probability that Sue makes her first basket on her 4th
            shot?
        </p>
    </statement>
    </task>

     <task workspace=".5in">
    <statement>
        <p>
              What is the probability that it takes no more than 8 shots before
            Sue makes her first basket?
        </p>
    </statement>
    </task>

     <task workspace=".5in">
    <statement>
        <p>
                What is the probability that it takes at least 10 shots before Sue
            makes her first basket?
        </p>
    </statement>
    </task>
</exercise>
   
   <exercise>
    <introduction>
        <p>
           A random variable <m>X</m> has space <m>\{1,2,3\}</m> and pmf given
            by <m>f(1)=0.2, f(2) = 0.5, f(3) = 0.3</m>. 
        </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="1in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                What is the moment generating function for <m>X</m>?
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="4in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Use the mgf to find the mean and variance of <m>X</m>. 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
   </exercise>
     <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>
              An electronic math placement tests consists of all multiple choice
            questions with 4 choices. The assessment continues as long as the
            person gets the correct answer. That is, it ends when the person
            gets the first wrong answer. A person is taking the test by randomly
            guessing answers. Let <m>X</m> be the number of the question the
            person first gets wrong.   
            </p>
        </introduction>
        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                     Find the pmf of <m>X</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

         <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                     What is the probability that <m>X</m> is 3?
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

         <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What is the probability that <m>X</m> is at least 4?
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

         <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What is the probability that <m>X</m> is no more than 6? 
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    
     </exercise>
         

</worksheet>